cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "NSS Yield Curve Engine"
abstract: >-
  A tested Python engine that fits the Nelson-Siegel-Svensson model to the U.S.
  Treasury par-yield curve, validates it against the Federal Reserve's curve, and
  uses it for recession signals, term premium decomposition (Adrian-Crump-Moench),
  arbitrage-free state-space forecasting (AFNS) and bond risk.
type: software
authors:
  - alias: RblxDev-ALS
repository-code: "https://github.com/RblxDev-ALS/NSS-Yield-Curve-Engine"
keywords:
  - yield curve
  - Nelson-Siegel-Svensson
  - term premium
  - fixed income
  - recession forecasting
version: 2.2.0
